q BT 65.20 771.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.748 Tw (Rosa Delgado had cleaned Don Vittorio Marchetti's house for twenty-two years, and in all that) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 750.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (time she had never once opened his piano.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 721.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.046 Tw (The piano stood in the study, black and gleaming, and every night at nine o'clock the Don sat) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 701.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.454 Tw (down at it and played the same song. He never told anyone what it was called. Rosa knew it by) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 680.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.729 Tw (heart anyway, because she had dusted that room while he played it for more than two decades,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 660.27 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (and some nights, when she was sure no one was listening, she hummed along.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 630.79 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.939 Tw (The Don died on a Tuesday. A heart attack, the doctor said, in his sleep, peaceful. His son) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 610.38 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.554 Tw (Antonio arrived from the city before the body was cold, and by Thursday the lawyer was) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 589.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (reading the will in the same study where the piano stood.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 560.49 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.256 Tw (Everything to Antonio. The house. The import business. The money. Rosa stood in the doorway) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 540.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.922 Tw (with a tray of coffee and listened to her own future disappear in one sentence, because a maid) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 519.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.244 Tw (who has served a family for twenty-two years does not inherit anything. She inherits a reference) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 499.27 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (letter, if she is lucky.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 469.79 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.544 Tw (Antonio did not even look at her. "Clear the house," he told her. "Everything goes. I am selling) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 449.38 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (the place.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 419.90 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.682 Tw (So on Friday morning, Rosa went to the study with her duster and her bucket, to clean a house) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 399.49 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.581 Tw (that was no longer her Don's. She dusted the piano last, the way she always did. And when she) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 379.08 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (lifted the lid to wipe the keys, one key stuck.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 349.60 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Middle C. It would not go down.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 320.12 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.353 Tw (Rosa pressed it again, harder, and something shifted inside the piano. A small wooden panel,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 299.71 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (hidden behind the keys, clicked open like a mouth.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 270.23 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.175 Tw (Inside, taped to the wood, was an envelope. Yellowed. Sealed. And on the front, in the Don's) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 249.82 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (own handwriting, four words:) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 220.34 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("For Rosa. Play the song.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 190.86 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.136 Tw (Her hands shook so badly she nearly dropped it. She had never seen the Don write her name.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 170.45 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Not once in twenty-two years. She tore the envelope open.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 140.97 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.487 Tw (Inside was a second will. Signed. Witnessed. Dated three months ago, by a lawyer whose name) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 120.56 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (she did not recognise. And under it, a letter, one page, in the same handwriting.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 91.08 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Rosa," it began. "You were the only honest person in this house.") Tj ET Q
