q BT 65.20 771.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Rosa read the will twice, because the first time she was certain she had misread it.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 741.91 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.494 Tw (The house did not go to Antonio. Half of the import business did not go to Antonio. They went) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 721.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.342 Tw (to Sofia Delgado. Nineteen years old. Rosa's daughter. The girl who had grown up doing her) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 701.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (homework at the kitchen table of this house, while the Don played his piano in the next room.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 671.61 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (And the letter said why.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 642.13 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.424 Tw (Twenty years ago, in a winter Rosa had spent her whole life trying to forget, the Don had come) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 621.72 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.102 Tw (to her room one night, and he had not come as a boss. Sofia was born nine months later. The) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 601.31 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.038 Tw (Don had never acknowledged her, not in public, not in private, not once. But he had watched her) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 580.90 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.516 Tw (grow up in his kitchen, and he had paid for her school in secret, and every night at nine o'clock) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 560.49 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.629 Tw (he had played the same song on the piano -- the song he had hummed to her mother the winter) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 540.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (she was conceived.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 510.60 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.312 Tw ("I could not give her my name while I lived," the letter said. "So I am giving her my house now) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 490.20 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.117 Tw (that I am dead. Antonio will fight it. He will say it is a forgery. He will say you stole it. Let him.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 469.79 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (The witnesses are real, and the truth is in the piano.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 440.31 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 3.190 Tw (Rosa stood in the study with the will in her hands and understood, for the first time in) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 419.90 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (twenty-two years, why the Don had played that song every single night.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 390.42 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (It was a lullaby. For his daughter.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 360.94 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.840 Tw (The study door opened. Antonio stood there, his phone in his hand, his face already impatient.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 340.53 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("What are you doing in here?" he said. "I told you to clear the house.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 311.05 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.553 Tw (Rosa slid the will into her apron pocket. Her heart was beating so loudly she was sure he could) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 290.64 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (hear it.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 261.16 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Just cleaning, Mr. Marchetti," she said. "The piano needed dusting.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 231.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.722 Tw (Antonio looked at the piano, then at her, and something in his eyes changed. He had grown up) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 211.27 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.860 Tw (in this house. He knew that piano. He knew his father played one song every night, and he) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 190.86 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (knew, the way sons always know, that his father had kept secrets from him.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 161.38 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Open the piano," he said quietly.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 131.90 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.806 Tw (Rosa's hand went to her apron pocket. In it was a piece of paper that made her daughter richer) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 111.49 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.354 Tw (than she had ever dreamed -- and made Rosa the most dangerous woman in the Marchetti) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 91.08 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (family.) Tj ET Q
